# Q: does the same weapon do measurably less to a Σοβιετικοί building than to a Κινέζοι one?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --armour-demo --probe tools/probe/armour.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/armour.txt
#
# Three Κέντρα Διοίκησης thirty metres apart — Σοβιετικοί, Κινέζοι, Δυτικοί — each with the same
# Σοβιετικοί Πυροβολείο thirty-five metres east of it. Same role, same hit points, same gun, same
# 45-damage shell, same reload; a different owner, and nothing else. The three headquarters stand on
# levelled sand with no canopy and no landform, so the ground they are judged on is the same ground,
# and their own `attributes` lines below are how that is checked rather than assumed.
#
# Armour is damage reduction per hit and not a bigger health pool, so what has to be read is the
# damage in the `events` stream — the same 45-damage shell arriving as three different numbers —
# and not how long each building survives. The `armour` query at the end prints the rule those three
# numbers come out of, per faction, and the two agreeing is the proof: a table that says 27/32/35
# above a stream that shows 27/32/35.
#
# This is the half of the design that makes a Σοβιετικοί base something you bring artillery to.
# The other half — the same factions' *vehicles*, which run the opposite way, and the mud that pays
# for them — is tools/probe/mud.probe.

# --- the line-up -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Six entities and nothing else: the three headquarters on slot 509 (Σοβιετικοί), 507 (Κινέζοι) and
# 505 (Δυτικοί), and the three guns that will shoot them on slot 508, 506 and 504.
units

# --- the ground, which must be the same under all three -------------------------------------------
# Sand, no vegetation, plain landform, cover 1000 ‰ for every movement class: the ground lets every
# point of every hit through, so nothing below is the terrain's doing.
attributes 4 -184
attributes 4 -154
attributes 4 -124

# --- the first shell on each -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every gun starts with its reload at zero, so one exchange has landed on all three by tick 55. Six
# events, three pairs: the same shot line and then the hit it produced.
tick 60
events 6

# --- five minutes of the same gun ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Six shells apiece. The health lines that follow are cumulative and would be equal if armour were
# not doing anything: three thousand and seventy-two points of damage aimed at each, arriving as
# considerably different amounts.
tick 240
events 30
unit 509
unit 507
unit 505

# --- the rule the three numbers come out of --------------------------------------------------------
# DamageRules.Compose, read for this role at this cell: the ground first, then the role's own
# construction times the owner's philosophy, floored at one. The three composed figures are the
# three damages in the stream above.
armour CommandCentre 4 -184 45

# --- the ledger of measurements --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read off the events stream and the armour query above, and re-read — not merely re-run — the day
# the armour figures move: these are the numbers this feature exists to produce, and a change to
# them is a balance decision rather than a regression.
#
# Before this change all three of these were 44 or 45, differing only by the cover of the cell each
# building happens to stand on. Now the difference is the owner, and it is a quarter of the shell.
expect "the same shell on a Σοβιετικοί headquarters" 27 27
expect "the same shell on a Κινέζοι headquarters" 35 35
expect "the same shell on a Δυτικοί headquarters" 32 32

# --- the composition rule itself, which all three call ---------------------------------------------
expect "Σοβιετικοί command centre: role × faction" 612 612
expect "Δυτικοί command centre: role × faction" 714 714
expect "Κινέζοι command centre: role × faction" 790 790

# --- and the other half of the design, which is not in this fixture ---------------------------------
# A Δυτικοί *vehicle* is the best-armoured thing on the map and a Σοβιετικοί one is the worst: the
# opposite ordering, on the same rule. Read here as arithmetic with a Κατιούσα's 95-damage shell,
# and in the field in mud.probe. The two light schools come out a point apart at this shell size,
# which is what "on a par with the Κινέζοι" looks like when it is a number rather than a phrase.
armour Tank 4 -154 95
